--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Provenance
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

lib/ainalrami/pairing.ex implements the FIDE Dutch system (C.04.3, 2026)
from the regulations, as specified in docs/dutch-cascade.md;
lib/ainalrami/weighted_matching.ex is a maximum-weight matching written for
this project from the published literature (Edmonds 1965; Galil 1986);
lib/ainalrami/trf.ex implements FIDE's published TRF specifications (C.04
Annex 2) and was adapted from the author's own OpenPairings project;
lib/ainalrami/sequence.ex implements Article 4 of C.04.3 (2026) directly
from the regulations. Releases up to and including 0.58.0 contained a
bracket cascade derived from BBP Pairings and carry that project's Apache
License 2.0 attribution; those releases keep it.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Not included in this repository
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

BBP Pairings (https://github.com/BieremaBoyzProgramming/bbpPairings) and
Gacrux / TieBreakServer (https://github.com/OttoMilvang/TieBreakServer) are
not vendored; they are located at runtime for comparison testing only.
